# Files prettier does not own.
#
# Prettier is a checker here (`cidx run code`) and a writer only on demand
# (`cidx run format`). Either way it has no business rewriting a file another
# tool generates: both would keep reformatting it, and whichever ran last would
# win (#272). `.gitignore` is honoured on top of this list — prettier reads both.

# Written by `cidx security baseline`. Its header says "do not edit by hand",
# and it promises that the same inputs produce the same bytes — a promise
# prettier's markdown-table realignment breaks on every run (#283, #286).
SECURITY-BASELINE.md

# Rewritten wholesale by commitizen at every `cz bump`.
CHANGELOG.md

# cidx's own hand-off artifacts: release notes written by `cidx release prepare`
# and the tag staging files. Generated, short-lived, not project source.
.cidx/

# Written by `cidx preset catalogue`, same contract as the baseline: generated,
# deterministic, regenerated by a test — prettier's table realignment would
# fight the generator on every run.
docs/reference/catalogue.md
